### Pull Request API Tests

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@token = YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
@githubToken = YOUR_GITHUB_TOKEN_HERE
@repoId = YOUR_REPOSITORY_ID_HERE

###############################################
### SETUP: Login first to get token
###############################################

### 1. Login to get JWT token
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "usernameOrEmail": "testuser",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

###############################################
### SYNC PULL REQUESTS FROM GITHUB
###############################################

### 2. Sync All Pull Requests for a Repository
# This fetches all PRs (open, closed, merged) from GitHub
POST {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 3. Sync Only Open Pull Requests
POST {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/sync?state=open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 4. Sync Only Closed Pull Requests
POST {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/sync?state=closed
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 5. Sync with Explicit GitHub Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/sync?state=all&token={{githubToken}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 6. Fetch Specific Pull Request by Number
# Example: Fetch PR #1
POST {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/fetch/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 7. Fetch Specific PR with GitHub Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/fetch/2?token={{githubToken}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

###############################################
### LIST PULL REQUESTS
###############################################

### 8. Get All Pull Requests for Current User
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 9. Get Open Pull Requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests?state=open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 10. Get Merged Pull Requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests?state=merged
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 11. Get Closed Pull Requests
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests?state=closed
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 12. Get All Pull Requests for Specific Repository
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 13. Get Open PRs for Specific Repository
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}?state=open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 14. Get Pull Request by ID (Use ID from previous responses)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/663f7b8a9e4c1d2a3b4c5d6e
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

###############################################
### STATISTICS & COUNTS
###############################################

### 15. Get Total Pull Request Count
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 16. Get Open PR Count
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/count?state=open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 17. Get Repository PR Count
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/count
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 18. Get Repository Open PR Count
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/count?state=open
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

###############################################
### ERROR CASES
###############################################

### 19. Sync Without GitHub Token (Should Fail if not in profile)
POST {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/sync
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 20. Fetch Non-Existent PR (Should Fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/{{repoId}}/fetch/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 21. Access Without Authentication (Should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests

###

### 22. Access Repository You Don't Own (Should Fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/invalid-repo-id
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

###############################################
### TESTING WORKFLOW
###############################################

# STEP 1: Setup
#   - Get GitHub Personal Access Token with 'repo' scope
#   - Login and get JWT token (Test #1)
#   - Get a repository ID from /repositories endpoint

# STEP 2: Update Variables
#   - Set @token to your JWT token
#   - Set @githubToken to your GitHub token
#   - Set @repoId to a valid repository ID

# STEP 3: Sync Pull Requests (Tests #2-7)
#   - This will fetch PRs from GitHub and save them

# STEP 4: List Pull Requests (Tests #8-14)
#   - View the synced PRs in various ways

# STEP 5: Get Statistics (Tests #15-18)
#   - Check counts and stats

# STEP 6: Test Error Cases (Tests #19-22)

###

